config BR2_PACKAGE_OZD
	bool "ozd"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC_TARGET_ARCH_SUPPORTS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC
	help
	  ozd on the board's own processing system: the associated
	  machine of the CADR in the fabric.  It answers the band's
	  file host and its time host, and it serves the host table.

	  A CADR has no file or time server in it, and neither has the
	  fabric and neither has cadr-chaosnet.  The host the band calls
	  is a machine on the network, and until now that machine had to
	  be somewhere else.  This package puts one on the board, so a
	  board with a card and no network is a whole site by itself:
	  the machine boots, asks for the time, is answered, and reaches
	  its files.

	  It is on unless the card turns it off with --no-ozd, and it
	  listens on the loopback and nowhere else.  ozd authenticates
	  nobody: any host that can reach its socket may read every root
	  and write every root that is not read-only.  The loopback is
	  therefore a decision and not a default, and a board that is to
	  serve a second machine has to be told to.

	  It is built from ozd's own source at the commit ozd.commit
	  pins, the way muir is, so no binary is carried in this
	  repository and ozd is never patched here.

comment "ozd needs a toolchain the Rust compiler supports"
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC_TARGET_ARCH_SUPPORTS
